IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cc-dates`
IMPORT `cc-rules`

-- County Court Act 1958 (Vic) -- the questions of the INDIVIDUAL PARTY to a civil proceeding in the County Court.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who is a party to a civil proceeding in the County Court, usually the plaintiff with a personal injury
-- or workers' compensation common law claim; also the parent or other person acting for an injured child (s 39A), the
-- individual on either side of a re-hearing (s 72), and the employee whose earnings are attached to pay a judgment (s 49A(3)).
-- "Can the County Court hear my claim?", "Can I recover more than I claimed?", "Can I settle my child's injury claim?",
-- "Where does my child's money go?", "Can I have a jury?", "Must I pay the jury fees?", "How much interest does my judgment
-- carry?", "Where does my appeal go?", "Can I get my fee waived?". The Court, the registrar and the defendant company get no
-- seat: the Court's and the registrar's findings, leave, opinions and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of cc-rules.l4. The
-- one rule with a deadline (s 72(3)) is a DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the County Court
-- Act 1958, Version No. 186 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
